+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` still reaches the caller as a rejection, and reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn, so `onError` fires with the session and the thrown error and `afterSession` fires before the session is saved — the point of the move being that a deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` no longer leaks the allocation on exactly the path where the allocation failed. `afterSession` runs on this path with no extra argument and no flag, so a hook cannot tell a session that never started from one that ran and failed: it may assume the turn was attempted, that no tool ran and that no provider call was made, and nothing more ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+
